{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "PTX, Vol. 2 appeals to me because Pentatonix's vocal harmonies connect with what I enjoyed about The New Old Fashioned.",
    "That choice recognizes that my interest can extend beyond Christmas albums when the vocal-group sound still feels connected."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Jim Reeves: Greatest Hits does not give me a clear reason to listen now; a broad collection is less appealing than a direct connection to my recent listening.",
    "Titles such as Road and 12 Stories give me too little evidence of the seasonal music or vocal harmonies I want, so I would skip them rather than explore."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "The choices seem to stretch my interest in a few particular albums into a much broader interest in music that I have not shown.",
    "Some recommendations seem to assume that another singer's album is a close enough match, while the vocal-group sound matters more to me right now."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My repeated Christmas listening suggests a specific seasonal interest, although those choices were made together in November 2014.",
    "My more recent choice of The New Old Fashioned makes vocal harmonies a stronger reason to choose something today than an unfamiliar title or a general greatest-hits collection."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "PTX, Vol. 2 connects with my current interest in vocal harmonies, but most of the other choices broaden my listening interests beyond what would motivate me to choose them."
}"}
